  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FairChain Moyee Coffee</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the last few decades, most of the added value in the Global Coffee Chain moved away from the coffee producing countries to the coffee consuming countries. Value adding activities lowered from 20% to 2% in Ethiopia.The goal of the project partners is to introduce the FairChain principles to the coffee sector in Ethiopia and start the first fully certified (a.o. organic, ISO 26000, HACCP) local premium coffee roasting facility for export purposes in Ethiopia. The joint venture will be the first one to operate under the FairChain concept, which will guarantee that the profits are fairly distributed among the entire value chain. Farmers will be paid a 20% premium on top of the commodity stock exchange price. Besides, smallholder coffee farmers will be trained in order to improve their performance in terms of using modern agro-techniques, quality improvement and higher yields.The coffee roasting facility will be located in Addis Ababa. Applicant of the project is Lampje Beheer B.V.. Partners are Moyee Coffee Ethiopia and Moyee Coffee Nederland B.V.. The partners will not set up a separate joint venture, as Moyee Coffee Ethiopia plc will execute the project. The present project will bring value adding activities in the coffee chain back in the coffee producing countries.</narrative>
  </description>
